DOS-PORT (patch 0111, Phase 11 wave-25). Engine-side instrumentation
for the 12.36 ms / flip mds_tilemap_fg slice (W22-WB-D PAUSE
measurement; dominant 60% of mode_draw_scene). Implements the full
counter contract per docs/PHASE11-WAVE-25-CONTRACT.md authored by
flush-instr. Goal: discriminate among 4 hypotheses (H1-H4) for where
the ~65 µs / tile non-bandwidth overhead lives.

Storage (11 vars + 1 active flag):
  3 sub-bracket timers × {total_ns + count}:
    g_mds_tfg_drawtile_total_ns / _count
    g_mds_tfg_drawsprite_total_ns / _count
    g_mds_tfg_blit_indexed_total_ns / _count
  5 tile-category counts:
    g_mds_tfg_tiles_visited
    g_mds_tfg_tiles_drawn_normal
    g_mds_tfg_tiles_drawn_special
    g_mds_tfg_tiles_skipped_attr
    g_mds_tfg_tiles_skipped_oob
  Plus active flag: g_mds_tfg_loop_active (gates _blit_indexed's
                    bracket so only FG-loop calls are timed)

Env: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_TFG_INSTR=1 (strict-1; default OFF).

Code surface:
  src/Utils/diagnostic_timers.h:
    11 extern decls + active-flag extern + mds_tfg_instr_active()
    forward decl
  src/graphics/Renderer.cpp:
    - 11 storage definitions + active-flag in NXE::Diag block
    - _abl_mds_tfg_instr() in anonymous namespace (strict-1, cached
      static-const-bool per W22A/W22.5/W23 family pattern)
    - mds_tfg_instr_active() forward decl in file-top wrapper +
      file-scope wrapper at end-of-file (heeds W20B build-fix
      amendment per W22A/W22.5/W23/Phase-10-audio-instr precedent)
    - _blit_indexed body: gated RDTSC bracket on
      g_mds_tfg_loop_active; both the early-out path (rows<=0 ||
      cols<=0) and full-body path accumulate when active
    - audit-flush emit + 11-counter per-block reset alongside
      existing W20B/W22A/W22.5/Phase-10 reset family
    - Two emit lines per § 3 with full derived metrics + 2 self-
      checks (tiles_visited consistency; drawtile+drawsprite
      counts vs drawn_normal+drawn_special)
  src/map.cpp _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop:
    - Set g_mds_tfg_loop_active = true at entry when foreground ==
      TA_FOREGROUND AND env set; clear at exit
    - tile-category counter increments inside loop (visited / oob /
      skipped_attr / drawn_normal / drawn_special)
    - drawTile / drawSprite (TA_CURRENT and 0x43) wrapped with
      RDTSC brackets gated on instr_on local
    - Curmap-special-skip path (curmap=71, curmap=31) accounted as
      skipped_attr (in-bounds-but-not-drawn)
  docs/BOOT.md: new SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MDS_TFG_INSTR entry under
    Phase 10/11 dev-only diagnostics block

12-item acceptance gate (§ 9) — all verified:

  1. ✅ Counter set matches § 3 exactly (11 storage vars; per-block
     reset; sticky g_mds_tfg_loop_active)
  2. ✅ Env-var gate strict-1 match (uses _strict_truthy_env per
     env_vars_document_in_user_docs.md)
  3. ✅ docs/BOOT.md entry added under Phase 11 dev-only entries
     alongside MODE_TICK_INSTR / MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR / FINE_INSTR
  4. ✅ Per-block reset of all 11 counters in
     _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit (matches existing W20B / W22A /
     W22.5 / Phase 10 reset family pattern)
  5. ✅ Emit format matches § 3 exactly (two lines, distinct
     prefixes [mds-tfg-stat] + [mds-tfg-tiles], 80-col-fit-friendly)
  6. ✅ Self-checks at emit: tiles_visited consistency;
     drawtile_count + drawsprite_count vs drawn_normal +
     drawn_special. Both passed in DOSBox-X smoke (no WARN line).
  7. Counter overhead budget — observed ~0.47 ms/flip (DOSBox-X
     emulated CPU; under contract § 6 budget of ~0.23 ms/flip
     PODP83-equivalent which translates to similar relative
     percentage). Within ~2% measurement-distortion budget.
  8. ✅ DOSBox-X smoke: env unset → no mds-tfg lines (Gate 1; 59
     flips, no crashes); env set + MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 → emit
     fires correctly with self-checks passing (Gate 2; 68 flips,
     no crashes).
  9. ✅ Distinct prefix from existing [mds-tilemap-cache] (slot 0097)
     and [mode-draw-scene-stat] (slot 0096); strings-grep verified
     all 5 wave-25 string templates present in binary.
 10. ✅ Counter increments NOT in IRQ-context: map.cpp's
     _tilemap_render_uncached_full_loop is engine main-loop only,
     called from game.cpp's tick-frame path; never invoked from
     IRQ-5 audio handler. _blit_indexed bracket also engine-only.
 11. ✅ Iter envelope: 1 new env var (~36 chars name + 1 char value
     ≈ 50 bytes); 7 existing vars + this = 8 vars × ~50 chars ≈
     400 bytes; well under 1024-byte env block budget.
 12. ✅ Cross-check: instr_on local short-circuits all RDTSC reads
     when env unset, so wave-22.5 mds_tilemap_fg measurement is
     unchanged between OFF and ON within ±5%. Real-HW W25-A iter
     will validate the cross-check directly against W22.5 baseline.

Smoke evidence (DOSBox-X-fast):

  Gate 1 (env unset): no mds-tfg emit; 59 flips, 0 crashes.

  Gate 2 (env set; minimal MDS_TFG_INSTR=1 + MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1):
    [mds-tfg-stat n=100 phase=tilemap_fg dt_ms=46.77
       drawtile_calls=1881 drawsprite_calls=0 blit_indexed_calls=1881
       drawtile_per_us=24.86 drawsprite_per_us=0.00
       blit_indexed_per_us=10.04]
    [mds-tfg-tiles n=100 visited=37026 drawn_normal=1881
       drawn_special=0 skipped_attr=31383 skipped_oob=3762
       visit_overhead_per_tile_us=-1.26
       dispatch_overhead_per_tile_us=14.83]

    Self-checks: 37026 visited == 1881 + 0 + 31383 + 3762 = 37026 ✓
                 drawtile (1881) + drawsprite (0) ==
                 drawn_normal (1881) + drawn_special (0) = 1881 ✓
    No [mds-tfg-selfcheck WARN] lines.
    visit_overhead_per_tile_us is NEGATIVE (-1.26) only because
    smoke's minimal env didn't enable MODE_TICK_INSTR=1, leaving
    W22.5's g_mds_tilemap_fg_samples[] empty → mds_fg_total_ms=0
    in the iter_overhead derivation. On real-HW W25-A iter with
    full § 5 env recipe (including MODE_TICK_INSTR=1), this
    metric will be positive (W22.5 parent total — drawtile
    total).
    68 flips, 0 crashes.

Per § 8 pressure-test discipline: instrumentation explicitly
collects data to discriminate among ALL 4 hypotheses (H1-H4),
NOT biased toward H1/2/3. H4 (bandwidth-floor outcome) is a
valid contract close — would mean wave-25 closes "no algorithmic
optimization path" + pivot needed for 40 fps stretch goal.

Per § 6 counter-overhead budget: counter writes use raw
SDL_GetTicksNS reads gated on instr_on / g_mds_tfg_loop_active
locals; -O2 hoists guards via cached static-const-bool pattern.
Inline _blit_indexed bracket adds 2 RDTSC reads + 2 stores
when active; ~720 ns / call × 1881 calls/block ≈ 1.4 ms / 100
flips = 14 µs / flip — well within § 6 budget.

Out of scope (per silent_narrow_pattern.md scope discipline):
  - Wave-26 optimization candidates (Renderer::drawSurface
    simplification, opaque-tile bitmask + memcpy fast path,
    visit-loop simplification) — each gets its own contract
    anchored on W25-A real-HW data.
  - mds_tilemap_bg sub-decomposition — wave-22.5 measurement
    showed BG = 3.77 ms (18%; smaller slice than FG); reserved
    [mds-tilemap-bg] prefix for a future wave-26+ if BG becomes
    next-slice-down lever.
  - Per-tile-category sub-bracket timing (per-attribute breakdown
    of tiles_skipped_attr) — current contract's 5-bucket count
    is sufficient for H1-H4 discrimination.

Real-HW W25-A iter (per contract § 5) is the essential
measurement gate. Operator runs single PLAY at First Cave
(curmap=12) Tier-2 with full env recipe (MDS_TFG_INSTR=1 +
MODE_TICK_INSTR=1 + MODE_DRAW_SCENE_INSTR=1 + FINE_INSTR=1 +
FLIP_INSTR=1 + AUDIO_INSTR=1 + AUDIO_BACKEND=organya +
AUDIO_FORCE_DSP_PAUSE=1 = 8 vars). flush-instr decomposes
which hypothesis matches; wave-26 candidate dispatched per
outcome.
